  {"heading":"Summary table / Tabla resumen",
   "segment_index":"S33.P1",
   "kind":"untrue",
   "en_span":"chapters/tables_descriptive.qmd:845-845",
   "tr_span":"chapters/tables_descriptive.es.qmd:843-843",
   "proposition":"The English says the tbl_summary() default converts missing values to \"Unknown\"; the Spanish says they are converted to \"Missing\".",
   "reader_consequence":"A Spanish reader expects the default table to label the missing category \"Missing\", but gtsummary prints \"Unknown\". The same page later states the default of missing_text = is \"Unknown\" (line 892), so the reader also meets a direct contradiction inside the chapter and cannot tell which default is real.",
   "confidence":"high"},
  {"heading":"Simple tabyl / Tabyl simple",
   "segment_index":"S9.P1",
   "kind":"missing",
   "en_span":"chapters/tables_descriptive.qmd:149-149",
   "tr_span":"chapters/tables_descriptive.es.qmd:147-147",
   "proposition":"The English states that the column tabyl() labels \"percent\" actually contains proportions; the Spanish drops the label-versus-content warning and says only that tabyl() returns proportions by column.",
   "reader_consequence":"A Spanish reader who runs linelist %>% tabyl(age_cat) sees a column headed percent holding values like 0.19 and has no text explaining the mismatch. They may read 0.19 as 0.19 percent instead of 19 percent.",
   "confidence":"medium"},
  {"heading":"janitor package / paquete janitor",
   "segment_index":"S8.P1",
   "kind":"untrue",
   "en_span":"chapters/tables_descriptive.qmd:145-145",
   "tr_span":"chapters/tables_descriptive.es.qmd:143-143",
   "proposition":"The English says the linelist is piped to janitor functions; the Spanish says it is piped to \"funciones de limpieza\" (cleaning functions), naming a package that does not exist.",
   "reader_consequence":"The bolded package name is the reader's pointer to what to install and load. A Spanish reader searching for a package called limpieza finds nothing, and cannot tell that tabyl() and the adorn_*() functions all come from janitor.",
   "confidence":"medium"},
  {"heading":"Percentiles",
   "segment_index":"S25.P1",
   "kind":"untrue",
   "en_span":"chapters/tables_descriptive.qmd:491-491",
   "tr_span":"chapters/tables_descriptive.es.qmd:489-489",
   "proposition":"The English says percentiles and quantiles deserve a special mention; the Spanish says percentiles and quartiles (\"cuartiles\").",
   "reader_consequence":"Quartiles are only the 25th, 50th and 75th percentiles. A Spanish reader may conclude quantile() covers quartiles only, when the very next sentence and the code use arbitrary probs values such as 0.05 and 0.98.",
   "confidence":"low"},
  {"heading":"Use on other tables / Uso en otras tablas",
